Loom: kernel.priority {level = N}, the issue priority of the current subgroup, lowered on AMDGPU to s_setprio.
The descriptor is an ordered execution barrier, so a pair of kernel.priority ops brackets the target instructions
between them; work meant to overlap with other code goes before the first one. Yah raises the iu4 GEMM fold to
priority 3: the folding wave's VALU wins issue arbitration over the other waves' WMMAs and it returns to its own
sooner. Bit-identical results; gu -2.8% cycles standalone, pp2048 GEMM cycles -1.1%.
